{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Yeshushum.</b> Some say the word lacks a bet, and thus it is yeshushu bam, and this is not correct, for what is the meaning of bam. The truth is that the mem is in place of a nun added in [certain] verb forms, like פדיום (Numbers 3:47). The meaning is that the land of Edom will be desolate alone, but the land of Israel the opposite. And according to the opinion of Rabbi Moses the Kohen, it is Jerusalem, the escaped one:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:45.970151834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}